      "updated_at": "2016-04-08T11:22:10Z",
      "body": "Ok so I have the following which works great, not sure if it the best way of doing it but as it works I'm happy.\n\nBasically your example was fine but meant that users of IE that had normal settings would lose their session once they closed the browser so would lose things such as their cart so I found that by trying to set a cookie and checking to see if it exists allows me to target users we these silly settings.\n\n```\nvar parser = require('ua-parser-js');\n\nmodule.exports = function(sails) {\n  return {\n\n    initialize: function(done) {\n      // Only relevant if the session hook is in use (refuse to continue lifting otherwise)\n      if (!sails.hooks.session) {\n        return done(new Error('In order for this `transient-sessions` hook to be meaningful, the `session` hook must be enabled.'));\n      }\n      return done();\n    },\n\n    routes: {\n      before: {\n        '/*': function(req, res, next) {\n          res.cookie('tryset',true, { maxAge: 900000, httpOnly: true });\n          var ua = parser(req.headers['user-agent']);\n          var isUserAgentSuspiciousOfTheWholeWorld;\n          if (ua.browser.name === 'IE' && !req.cookies.tryset) {\n            isUserAgentSuspiciousOfTheWholeWorld = true;\n          } else if (ua.browser.name === 'IE' && req.cookies.tryset) {\n            req.session.cookie.expires = 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000 * 30;\n          }\n\n          if (isUserAgentSuspiciousOfTheWholeWorld) {\n            req.session.cookie.expires = false;\n          }\n          return next();\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  };\n};\n```\n",
